<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We used the default parameters of the DreamerV3 XL model. <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\mathrm{CDP}}=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>CDP</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\mathrm{CDP}}=500</annotation></semantics></math>. The predictor was a two-layer MLP with 8192 input units, 4096 hidden units, and 4096 output units. The training ratio was 32 instead of 512. The learning rate of the RSSM, and the predictor were <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\cdot 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\cdot 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> and the learning rate of the encoder was <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\cdot 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\cdot 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>. The other networks were trained with a learning rate of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\cdot 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\cdot 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Supplementary Figures</h3>

<figure id="A1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07083v1/success_rate.png" id="A1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/308;" width="548" height="308" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.1: </span>Crafter score for Dreamer (Blue) and Dreamer-CDP (purple) for each achievement.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07083v1/abl1.png" id="A1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:411/238;" width="411" height="238" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.2: </span>Comparison between Dreamer-CDP (Purple) and several ablations. Orange: Ablation of the reward and value gradient to train the world model. Most of the learning signal comes from the latent space predictive loss. Green: Ablation of <math id="A1.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CDP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CDP</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{CDP}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dyn/rep}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>dyn</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>rep</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{dyn/rep}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <abbr title="" class="ltx_glossaryref ltx_missing">KL</abbr> balancing is not sufficient to train the world model in the latent space. Black: CDP loss alone also results in lower cumulative return. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
